0023: the server's view of a client texture (real-time GI work package WP11). Client export RemixBridge_GiPixelView(src, dst) sends Bridge_GiPixelView with two texture ids; the server's GiPixelPass::view (native/remix-bridge/gi/gi_pixel_pass.h) blits the renderer's image of src into dst through DXVK's ID3D9VkExternalPass, in stream order (nearest at the same size, linear otherwise), so the G-buffer's albedo + id target reaches the server's Vulkan device. Views and refused views are two words of the GiPixel shared block (views, viewFaults) and a [GiPixel] views= log line. Runs only when the per-pixel pass is on. Test: test_gi_pixel_device (test-gi-pixel.cmd) checks a same-size and a quarter-size view of a two-colour A8R8G8B8 target and a refused depth source.
Applies after 0022.
